    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "First win",
          "heading": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 in Udine for first Nations Championship win",
          "body": "The 21-16 result in Round 6 closed both sides' pool campaigns at Udine's Bluenergy Stadium, and Jake White's side had arrived without a Nations Championship victory after fading in the second half of a 43-15 defeat by Ireland. Italy were weakened late: OnRugby reported tighthead Simone Ferrari suffered a left upper-limb injury an hour before kickoff, with Marco Riccioni promoted to start and Ion Neculai added to the bench."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Record win",
          "heading": "Slade opens scoring as England beat All Blacks by record margin",
          "body": "Fin Smith's grubber put Henry Slade over after four minutes at Allianz Stadium. Jack van Poortvliet and Ben Earl added first-half tries as England led 19-0 after 36 minutes, and Ollie Chessum crashed over for the fourth soon after the restart. The 37-12 result, five tries to two, was England's biggest winning margin over New Zealand, eclipsing 2012's 38-21, Planet Rugby noted. The Guardian added that it came despite Tommy Freeman's pre-game injury withdrawal."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Stade de France tribute",
          "heading": "French federation's Argentina-match tribute to Federico Martin Aramburu enlists Antoine Dupont",
          "body": "Aramburu's son was named to walk out before France-Argentina in an Argentina jersey, holding the hands of both captains, Dupont and hooker Julián Montoya, in honour of his dual nationality, Rugbyrama reported. The former Argentine player, well known in the French championship in the early 2000s, was murdered in Paris in 2022 by two far-right activists. They were later jailed for 26 and 19 years. The federation also scheduled a minute's applause in his memory at Saint-Denis."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ireland XV",
          "heading": "McCarthy and Ryan score twice as Ireland XV rout Fiji Latui",
          "body": "Ireland's second string, the Ireland XV, met little resistance at Virgin Media Park in Cork on Friday night as Fiji Latui collected four yellow cards and a red card in the first half, at one point dropping to 12 men. Captain Gus McCarthy and Connacht's Daniel Ryan crossed twice apiece in a nine-try win, while Joey Carbery set up Ryan's opener and dived under the posts for one of his own. Paul Boyle withdrew from the bench with a neck issue; Scott Penny replaced him."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Quesada handed Miotti his debut at fly-half before Italy's Fiji defeat",
          "body": "Wing injuries to Lynagh, Faissal, Pani and Trulla shaped the call, Quesada explained before Saturday's 16-21 loss to Fiji in Udine. Ange Capuozzo moved to the wing and Tommaso Allan to full-back so Domingo Miotti could debut at No. 10. Quesada denied it was a snub of Paolo Garbisi, who knew Miotti would come in after the previous two tests. He also said a debut in a key position is easier from the start. Alessandro Ortombina replaced Federico Ruzza as lineout leader."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "OnRugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Breakout star",
          "heading": "Liam McConnell scores hat-trick on third Scotland appearance in Japan rout",
          "body": "The 22-year-old Edinburgh back-rower was the standout of Saturday's 11-try, 67-5 win at Murrayfield, and BBC Scotland chief sports writer Tom English called him electrifying in attack and defence alike. English noted the long-running frustration among McConnell's backers at his lack of Scotland opportunities. His second try came early in the second half from Darcy Graham's kick through, chase and offload. Graham's own hat-trick took his international try tally to 41."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rotation call",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy rotated Wales for Wallabies after 300 tackles against All Blacks",
          "body": "Wales went into Saturday's Nations Championship test against Australia in Cardiff with a changed side. Tandy cited the 300 tackles and high ball-in-play time of the New Zealand win. Sam Costelow and Tomos Williams formed the half-back pairing, Blair Murray started at full-back and Dewi Lake captained the side, while Joe Hawkins and Louie Hennessey were named among the replacements. Tandy said: \"The guys played outstanding against the All Blacks but we’ve got guys who are fresh and hungry.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
