      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Edwards' defence",
          "heading": "Rugbyrama flags flaws France knew in Shaun Edwards' Pumas defensive system",
          "body": "Before Saturday's Nations Championship meeting at the Stade de France, Midi Olympique's Nicolas Zanardi argued that six years under Edwards, now in charge of the Pumas' defence, left Les Bleus fluent in his demands: a 13-man front line, double tackles to kill offloads and no easy ruck ball. He cited weak points France had felt first-hand, notably forwards left to fend for themselves after lineouts, and asked whether Tomás Albornoz would be targeted. France lineout coach Laurent Sempéré said Edwards had surely evolved too, adapting to his new colleagues."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
        }
      ],
