      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Les Kiss left Fraser McReight on the bench for Wales test",
          "body": "Carlo Tizzano got the nod in a back row captained by Harry Wilson alongside Rob Valetini as Australia faced Wales at the Principality Stadium on Saturday night. Carter Gordon and Ryan Lonergan formed the halves, with Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii and Len Ikitau in midfield. Kiss's bench ran five forwards to three backs, McReight joined by Billy Pollard, Angus Bell, Allan Alaalatoa and Jeremy Williams. Frenchman Luc Ramos took the whistle."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Scotland thrash Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick. Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
