    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline",
          "heading": "Harada hip drop and Stolberg tackle bring Japan two Murrayfield yellows",
          "body": "Both offences came from replacements in the closing quarter of Saturday's 67-5 defeat by Scotland. Mamoru Harada was sin-binned in the 69th minute for a hip-drop tackle, and Michael Stolberg followed in the 79th for an early tackle, Planet Rugby reported. Scotland's 11 tries included hat-tricks for Liam McConnell and Darcy Graham. Japan's only reply was Takuro Matsunaga's unconverted 53rd-minute try, scored after a box kick bounced awkwardly and eluded Kyle Rowe."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 for record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. South Africa seek misconduct hearing over banned Rassie Erasmus."
