      }
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Record defeat",
          "heading": "All Blacks slump to record 37-12 defeat by England at Twickenham",
          "body": "Dave Rennie's side were beaten by 25 points at Allianz Stadium on Saturday, eclipsing England's previous best margin in the fixture — 38-21 in 2012 — and handing them successive wins over New Zealand for the first time since 2002 and 2003. Ethan de Groot and Beauden Barrett, in his 150th Test, scored the tries. According to SA Rugby Magazine, the result leaves the Springboks needing one log point against Ireland in Dublin to top the southern hemisphere standings and claim a place in the final."
        },
